# Rendering & performance

- Canvas2D, layered: static edge layer (once per graph) / dynamic settle-fill (dirty-rect batched) / overlay layer (frontier, pivots, forest) / FX layer (blooms, photo-finish).
- Perf budget: 60fps on 5k nodes; ≥30fps on 100k. No main-thread stalls > 50ms during a 3-lane 25k race. ≥25k nodes: aggregated path — 2px ImageData nodes, offscreen prerendered edge bitmap.
- Trace generation always in workers, streamed in chunks (transferables); playback must be able to start before generation finishes.
- Everything must be scrub-safe both directions: state at clock T must be identical whether reached by playing forward or scrubbing back (keyframe snapshots ~every 250k ops).
- Renderer reads decoded TraceEvents only — never import from src/core algorithm modules.
- Visual language (design.md §3.6): one perceptually-uniform colorblind-safe settle gradient shared by lanes; lane accents marble/ember/moss; dark default + light; tabular numerals for counters; no chartjunk.
